          "file": "fpd-drive-future-policy-distillation-figure-1.png",
          "width": 814,
          "height": 520,
          "format": "png",
          "originalHtmlCaption": "Figure 1:  Overview of FPD-Drive. \nThe teacher–student framework employs a common coarse-to-fine architecture comprising a visual encoder, a proposal decoder, a diffusion refiner, and a scorer (Sec.  3.1 ).\nRecorded future observations additionally guide the teacher’s refinement and scoring (Sec.  3.2 ).\n Future-Privileged Multi-Target Distillation  transfers high-quality, geometrically diverse trajectories selected from evaluated teacher candidates to supervise the student’s proposal decoder and refiner (Sec.  3.3 ).\n Safety-Aware Score Correction  uses evaluated student candidates to penalize highly ranked unsafe trajectories relative to nearby safe alternatives and increase confidence in underestimated safe candidates (Sec.  3.4 ).\nOnly the student is used at deployment.",
          "actualImageViewed": true,
          "viewMethod": "tools.view_image displayed full saved original; manual visual inspection",
          "visualObservation": "Teacher upper branch has current and future images; student lower branch has only current images. Lower panels show target diversity and unsafe/safe score correction."
        },
